# INT n/INTO/INT3/INT1 -- override
# The manual's Operation (some 400 lines) is the full protected-mode and
# IA-32e interrupt delivery; v1 delivers every exception and software
# interrupt through one microcode routine, routines/DELIVER.sdm (the IA-32e
# branch of this Operation for a 64-bit interrupt gate at CPL 0). What's
# left here is raising the vector as a trap (the saved RIP is the next
# instruction). INT1 (ICEBP) raises #DB as a trap and, like INT3, is not
# checked against the gate's DPL (Vol. 3A 19.3.1.2... treated here as #DB).
@operation
IF instruction is INT3
    THEN #BP;
    ELSE IF instruction is INT1
    THEN #DB;
    ELSE RaiseVector(SRC);
FI;
